WEBVTT

NOTE Fair Split film, script v4: closed captions, word for word with every spoken line and never burned in (video/proto/STYLE.md §8). Generated from video/script.ts by video/build.mjs. Timed to the recorded voice (Gemini TTS narration, aligned offline) and the member's own sentence.

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:06.882
Picture a co-op paying sixty-four cacao
farmers from handwritten weigh-slips.

2
00:00:06.882 --> 00:00:11.252
A duplicate,
or a fine no rule allows, goes unseen.

3
00:00:11.252 --> 00:00:13.950
Members can't check it. Nor can the buyer.

4
00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:17.090
Fair Split: Claude reads the paper.

5
00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:21.010
Code computes every amount
and holds what it can't justify.

6
00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:23.306
Two officers sign large batches.

7
00:00:23.306 --> 00:00:27.040
A simulated PayPal pays.
The buyer re-checks everything.

8
00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:35.030
Slips go to Claude, then a deterministic
engine; two keys sign.

9
00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:40.920
A PayPal invoice funds it; simulated
PayPal Payouts pay members, safe to retry.

10
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.301
Highlights:
a split matrix that rebalances;

11
00:00:47.301 --> 00:00:50.996
a frozen rate card; two keys, one hash;

12
00:00:50.996 --> 00:00:55.740
proof in your browser;
pay you can hear; Try to break it.

13
00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:04.110
Each slip has a pink carbon copy.
Photograph both, and it counts twice.

14
00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.240
Lantern Bay, the chocolate buyer,

15
00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:12.180
pays one invoice through PayPal's
Agent Toolkit, on a simulated sandbox.

16
00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:16.400
Claude's real reading of one slip.

17
00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:19.860
The run itself replays
a labelled stand-in;

18
00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:22.730
Analyn types one stained digit by hand.

19
00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:28.518
Counted once, the duplicate's money
returns to the other sixty-three members,

20
00:01:28.518 --> 00:01:30.970
and the dial drops inside the limit.

21
00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:37.254
Two more holds go to a person.
Analyn tries a deduction.

22
00:01:37.254 --> 00:01:41.200
Refused: the rate card was
locked before the first slip.

23
00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:45.320
Above three hundred dollars, two keys:

24
00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:49.870
Analyn signs; the Chair co-signs
the same batch hash on his phone.

25
00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:56.009
The simulated PayPal accepts the batch:
sent, not yet paid.

26
00:01:56.009 --> 00:02:00.020
Seven items confirm;
a member without PayPal moves to cash.

27
00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:05.151
Lantern Bay opens Proof
and re-checks the rate card,

28
00:02:05.151 --> 00:02:07.220
both signatures and every line.

29
00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:13.540
Her pay traces to four slips.
It plays in Cebuano.

30
00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:15.522
[Cebuano: machine-translated,
pending native review] Premium gikan sa

31
00:02:15.522 --> 00:02:18.300
Lantern Bay Chocolate Co.:

32
00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:22.330
forty-three dollars and sixty-nine cents,
walay kaltas.

33
00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:29.028
Underneath: over five thousand
automated tests and three kill switches.

34
00:02:29.028 --> 00:02:33.480
Others we found share parts;
none starts from a handwritten weigh-slip.

35
00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:39.223
The limits: PayPal is a simulated sandbox;
no real farmer was paid.

36
00:02:39.223 --> 00:02:43.850
Synthetic people and slips.
A replayed stand-in. Gemini TTS voices.

37
00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:47.400
Members check their own pay;

38
00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:53.080
the buyer traces its premium.
Every peso, traced to the pencil mark.
